# W44-97 per-strategy AC tokenization dump on 7 OPEN cells post W44-96
# =====================================================================
#
# Follow-on to W44-92 (per-strategy dump of 3 toughest cells in the 13-OPEN
# state). W44-96 (`76d1dfd7`) shipped the zenanalyze sub-discriminator
# (edge_density>=0.7 AND fcbr<0.01) routing 1420710/1531677 onto the variant Z
# table (dct32x32=1.20 instead of 1.34) at d>=4.5. That closed 6 of 13 cells:
# 1420710 e6 d5, e6 d6, e8 d5, e9 d5 and 1531677 e5 d6, e6 d6. The 7 remaining
# OPEN cells need a different attack.
#
# Cells (7 total, sorted by bytes_delta_pct descending):
#   1) 1420710 e5 d=6:  +4.02%  (24114→21004 vs cjxl 20192)
#   2) 1531677 e9 d=5:  +3.64%  (19486 vs cjxl 18802)
#   3) 1420710 e5 d=5:  +3.67%  (24114 vs cjxl 23261)
#   4) 1531677 e5 d=5:  +3.54%  (20944 vs cjxl 20227)
#   5) 1420710 e7 d=5:  +3.36%  (24437 vs cjxl 23643)
#   6) 1531677 e8 d=5:  +3.05%  (19412 vs cjxl 18838)
#   7) 1531677 e6 d=5:  +3.04%  (21185 vs cjxl 20560)
#
# Method
# ------
# Reuses W44-76/W44-92 infrastructure: `JXL_W44_76_PER_BLOCK_DUMP=<dir>` env
# var on both cjxl-rs (built from `76d1dfd7` shared-target main) and libjxl
# (`w44-76-per-block-debug` branch, build at
# `~/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl--w44-76-per-block-debug-dump`). Per-block dump
# fields: (bx, by, strategy_wire, channel, nzeros, qac).
#
# Analysis: `benchmarks/w44_92_per_strategy_dump.py` (unchanged).
# Aggregation: `/tmp/w44_97_aggregate.py` (built fresh for cross-cell view).
#
# OUTPUT FILES
# ------------
# benchmarks/w44_97_per_strategy_dump_post_w44_96_2026-05-19.tsv (this dump,
#     56 data rows = 7 cells × ~8 strategies)
# benchmarks/w44_97_per_strategy_dump_post_w44_96_2026-05-19.meta (this file)
#
